WEBVTT

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.310
"Operation: Ares"

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:37.970
Did you call for me?

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.090
Please take a look at this.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.500
We're investigating a Wulgaru 
capital ship that crashed on Mars?

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.300
Right. It would be too much 
for the GDF to handle.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.420
Besides, up-to-date information 
is highly valuable.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.210
This is going to be an 
infiltration operation.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:56.780
Infiltration?

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:57.630
Where is the target?

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.630
After the Battle of Ceres,

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.910
we found an enemy craft 
that crash landed on Mars.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.230
Team Rabbits is to infiltrate the 
ship and retrieve any data you can.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.260
We've never undergone training for this!

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.150
Sounds cool, like spy stuff!

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.460
Silence! Izuru Hitachi!

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:15.130
Ma'am!

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.090
Toshikazu Asagi!

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:16.840
Ma'am!

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.930
You will use your core 
units in this mission.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.910
You will infiltrate the enemy ship 
while the other three offer support.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.350
Roger!

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.520
Do you have blueprints for 
the inside of the enemy ship?

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.520
Allow me to explain.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.510
Master Daneel!

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.120
Your target is in the 
Valles Marineris on Mars.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.580
It was found hanging on 
the edge of the precipice.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.960
The Marimari what...?

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.820
The Marineris!

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.260
It's 4,000km long and 7km deep.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.440
It's a massive ravine that 
cuts from East to West

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.650
along the center of Mars.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.920
Thank you for the explanation.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:02.220
As things stand, we expect the 
target to plummet into the ravine

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.560
or collapse under its own 
weight due to the gravity.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:08.200
At best, we believe to 
have 36 hours remaining.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.060
That's plenty of time!

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.650
Even if we left for Mars immediately,

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.130
carrying out the mission 
is going to take some time.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.440
Precisely.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.790
The target may also deteriorate

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.510
quicker than anticipated due 
to unforeseen circumstances.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:22.950
Enemy interference is 
also a possibility.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.370
As such, I want this mission 
over within 24 hours.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.390
That doesn't give us much time.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.910
You have twelve hours to 
prepare and get there.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.330
After which you have six hours 
to break in and pull out.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.250
Ma'am!

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.400
I have transferred blueprints of the 
enemy ship to each of your units.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.550
I shall also accompany you.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:43.130
Henceforth, this mission will be 
referred to as Operation: Ares!

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:46.200
The operation begins at 1800 hours.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.950
You are free to spend the 
next six hours resting.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.390
Roger!

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.500
Where did these guts come from?

00:03:58.900 --> 00:03:59.940
Space squid, probably.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:00.820
For reals?!

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:02.530
They're caught in the Star Rose.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.090
Didn't you know?

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.460
The outer walls are dual layered 
with water in the middle

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:08.390
to protect us from 
hazardous cosmic rays.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.850
We raise consumable fish along 
with other forms of sea life.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.920
Wow! I never knew!

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.070
Is that where the boiled mackerel 
I had for breakfast came from?

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.130
We catch them up here.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.080
Missy!

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.510
We also farm other fish 
like tuna and yellowtail.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.390
Did you come to see me?!

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.640
No, I wouldn't say-

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.200
Right, right! We came to see you, Kitty.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.670
This contains data regarding 
the anticipated weather

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:35.960
on Mars in 48 hours.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:38.720
There is a strong ferric oxide 
storm, which will limit

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:40.880
your AHSMB unit's maneuverability.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.820
Although I'm sure this will be 
a piece of cake for you, Kitty.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.430
Let's celebrate when you 
get back safe and sound.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.410
Mew!

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.750
He's got Tamaki eating from 
the palm of his hand...

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.820
He's motivating her by dangling 
a carrot in front of her nose...

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.420
Increasing backup engine's output.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.000
Disconnect all equipment.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.380
AUP activated.
Disconnect all equipment.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:00.500
Start all engines!

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.340
External power has been established.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.380
Internal pressure increasing. 
Turbines activated.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.930
Main engine, military!

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.320
Blast off!

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.610
Is it all ready to go?

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.990
Hey, did you hear me?

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:28.610
Yeah, save it for later.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.200
We're checking our records.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.640
Go get a clue!

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:35.020
Jeez! You've totally 
ruined my good mood.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.250
Why did my pit crew have 
to be them of all people?

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.460
3D girls bite.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.380
Uh-huh...

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:50.570
Izuru Hitachi has risen 
to Harmonic Level 6...

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.000
That is too sharp of an increase...

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.020
My! Tamaki's is also increasing.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:59.500
It looks like this fluctuates 
dramatically based on their mental state.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.380
Commence the operation!

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:46.320
Huh? It feels like I'm 
getting pulled down.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.470
We're dropping faster 
than I had expected.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:53.160
The surface gravity 
on Mars is 3.71 m/s².

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:55.560
It's a little over a third of 
Earth's gravity, so be careful!

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.240
Plus we've got some nasty winds!

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.110
This doesn't bug me at all!

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:01.560
Then you're the only one 
who isn't having issues!

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:03.040
Found it!

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.480
Tamaki, scout it out.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:07.650
Roger!

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.170
Some bogeys came out!

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:34.850
They fell down all on their own.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.510
I've identified enemy fighters 
around the capital ship!

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.310
I can't see them through this storm!

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.580
Kei, what is the situation 
around the target?

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.220
The magnetic properties 
of the ferric oxide storm

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:47.780
have rendered my radar 
and sensors inoperable.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:48.960
Not cool...

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.900
Tamaki, bring them over here.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.280
Sure thing.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.580
Gold 4, prepare to fire!

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:58.270
Roger!

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:04.860
No evasive maneuvers? 
They dropped like flies!

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.960
They're headed your way.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.590
Did that attack give 
our location away...?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.070
What were you thinking, Suruga?!

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.570
Izuru told me to draw them over here!

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.660
Sneak in while we draw their attention.

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:18.100
Good idea!

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.250
Leave these wimps to me!

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:23.270
I appreciate it.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:33.970
It's hard to move in this...

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.740
The sand is thicker than 
expected, isn't it?

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.630
How come she's the only one who 
can move around like normal?

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:39.740
Isn't her enthusiasm great?

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:41.390
That's the difference?

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:44.830
Her unit won't last long 
if she keeps that up.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.500
Found it!

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:49.960
It's guarded!

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:54.700
Laser sights are ineffective.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.340
Shifting the range finder 
from auto to manual.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.080
Dropping the convergence 
value from 155 to 120.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:01.220
Amending for +2.12G.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.490
Inserting the anticipated 
trajectory deviations.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.290
We're goin' manual, huh? 
This is getting fun!

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.710
I'm aimin' for targets that I can't 
see based solely off of speculation!

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:13.020
This is when a sniper gets 
to show what he's made of!

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:16.410
I'm all set!

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:17.550
Fire!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.180
He got all of them!

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.360
Whatcha think of my moves?

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:28.110
You were just following 
Kei's orders, weren't you?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:30.110
Yeah, but still!

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.670
Let's sneak in while we still can!

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.900
It would seem you've successfully 
infiltrated the ship.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.760
I shall lead the way from here.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.540
The bridge is this 
way. Please follow me.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:54.340
W-wait a second! I need 
to set our transponder.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.860
We'll leave you behind 
if you don't hurry!

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:01.640
It looks like it's alive...

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:05.120
Yeah. I hate how it feels 
like we're inside an animal!

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:09.210
The construction materials 
used biological tissues.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.290
But it's starting to fall apart...

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.690
I imagine it is starting to deteriorate.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:15.050
Let's hurry.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.760
It's the enemy! Fire!

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.920
That is no longer necessary.

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:30.600
It's dead?

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:33.630
If it wasn't, you would be!

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.310
They are unable to move 
without a cartridge.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:39.410
A cartridge?

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:43.910
Correct. They were cloned 
together with their units.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.760
However, without this cartridge,

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:48.280
the organic part of their unit cannot

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.830
sustain itself beyond 
a given period of time.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:52.620
Foot soldiers are consumable resources,

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:56.170
so I imagine they were cut from the 
cartridge supplies after the crash.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.210
Clones are consumable resources...?

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:02.990
We use the genes from past prize 
soldiers to mass produce their clones.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:07.760
Thus they can continue to hunt 
in pursuit of superior genes.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.360
And their target is...

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.500
Correct. It is you.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:17.430
The storm above the target 
appears to be growing worse.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.550
Is it interfering with the mission?

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:22.220
Currently, they are unable to 
use their radar or sensors.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.260
Transmissions have entered the red.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:27.610
Their maneuverability 
has dropped by 20%.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.500
The target's rate of deterioration 
may increase as well.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:34.330
So the operation itself is in peril...

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:37.900
Tell them that they may withdraw 
at their own discretion

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:40.110
if Maneuverability Levels 
drop to 40% or lower.

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:41.740
Roger. I'll tell them.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.420
Air turbulence is increasing.

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:46.020
I am having a hard time getting through.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:47.900
Continue sending the transmission.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:50.850
We can't afford to lose 
them over this mission.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:58.330
Do you copy? This is Godinion.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.400
I hear ya!

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:02.180
Is that you, Kitty? 
What is the situation?

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.410
Izuru and Asagi went inside, mew!

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.240
Really? Please relay this to everyone.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:10.680
"You are to pull back if 
maneuverability drops to 40%."

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.690
Roger!

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:14.040
That aside, how about 
we go out to eat when

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:15.270
you successfully complete this mission?

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:18.380
Then please eat some pickled 
fish guts with me, mew!

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:20.390
That'll be a piece of cake.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:23.300
What is with that, "mew," crap?

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:30.540
It's been a while since this 
ship crashed, hasn't it?

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.000
So it would seem.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:35.380
Why didn't they evacuate 
before they died?

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.910
The foot soldiers you have

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:40.510
been seeing only move in 
accordance with their orders.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:44.090
Their superior commanders probably 
either fled or perished.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:47.280
So they carried out their 
orders until their cartridges

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.980
ran out and they died?

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:50.100
Precisely.

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:52.160
Didn't they think of 
abandoning the ship?

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:55.920
Only a select handful of 
Manaava- Excuse me, Wulgaru,

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.240
are capable of free thought.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:02.130
Those of the soldier class do 
not possess wills of their own.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:05.550
That's horrible...! Aren't 
they living beings?

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:08.520
What would you do when a machine breaks?

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:11.160
I'd fix it.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.620
And if you couldn't?

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:16.560
I'd throw it away.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:18.070
Exactly.

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:21.590
That is precisely how the 
Wulgaru view the soldier class.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:25.560
Those who lack wills of their 
own are naught but robots.

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:29.810
It would seem that this 
does not sit well with you.

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:30.790
Right...

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:35.490
That is what Lady Teoria said 
as well when she defected.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.730
She said, "Is a life not a life?"

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:46.710
It would seem that the ship is 
deteriorating faster than anticipated.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:48.900
Let us hurry.

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:53.830
Is this the bridge?

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:55.730
Correct.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:58.910
Daneel, will you be all 
right without a suit?

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.520
My body has been refortified.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.260
Wait!

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:16.910
I'm going in first!

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.060
What are you doing?

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.740
Could you please keep your distance?

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.250
I am going to memorize this; 
you are distracting me.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:44.020
You're memorizing it...?

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:47.240
Yes. Sheer quantity will not 
prove to be problematic,

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.100
although this may take some time.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:54.080
Changes sighted in the target!

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:55.580
Zoom in!

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.190
Its deterioration has 
begun to accelerate?

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:03.110
It is worse than we had anticipated.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:05.990
This is bad. Tell them to hurry!

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:06.770
Roger.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.420
This is Guiliano.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:11.650
Kitty, can you hear 
me? It's me, Guiliano.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.350
Why don't you just say her name?

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:18.180
We received a report from the 
medical clinic that this is

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.310
better for that pilot's 
mental state of being.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:21.270
Seriously?

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.920
You're the only one we 
can count on, Kitty.

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.240
Could you relay that to the other 
team members on the surface?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.090
Mew!

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:32.870
I'm counting on you.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:36.700
Rose 3's Harmonic Levels are increasing.

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:38.350
It's legit!

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:44.390
I'm amazed she can move around 
like that in this environment.

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:45.830
But her unit can't take 
much more of this!

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:47.090
Kei, do you copy?

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.800
Sure do. What is the situation?

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:51.870
Master Daneel is in danger! We 
have to hurry and let him know!

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:53.510
How about Izuru and Asagi?

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:55.620
A transmission from the transponder?

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:56.990
What's she say?

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:59.100
The target's deterioration 
is accelerating.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.270
Hurry and pull out!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:03.150
We can't move yet. Wait a bit!

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.710
Get out as soon as you can!

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:05.980
Roger!

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.900
I'll admit this doesn't look good.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:09.360
Look out!

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:14.280
We'll have to protect 
him until he's done.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:17.060
It could cause problems if we 
hit some of the stuff in here.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:18.950
Only hit the debris 
that is falling down!

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.330
Talk about a pain...

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:24.750
What area caved in?!

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:26.670
The passageway!

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:31.160
It's no use! This route has 
been completely buried!

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:32.320
How about the other passageways?

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.910
I can't say! Let's take a look!

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:40.770
The target...!

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:41.680
It collapsed!

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:43.900
The target has reached dangerous levels.

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:45.340
Pull out immediately!

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:47.200
Infiltration Team, pull out!

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.400
I repeat: Infiltration Team, pull out!

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.920
The transponder is not 
receiving our transmissions!

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.320
What is the Infiltration Team's status?

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.390
This is Tamaki! Please respond.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.940
This is Godinion. Please 
update us on the situation.

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:05.290
The capital ship collapsed!

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:06.950
That's what I saw.

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:09.320
Kitty, your unit is about 
to reach its limit.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:10.320
Please pull back.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:11.610
But-!

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:14.240
This is Izuru! This is Izuru!

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:16.090
Someone, anyone, please respond!

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:16.910
Izuru!

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:19.350
Send this information 
to Suruga immediately.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.070
Please have him fire at 
the indicated coordinates!

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:24.080
Did you hear that, Kei?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.100
Sure did! Send over the data.

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:28.400
Confirming the coordinates.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.820
Preparing to fire at full power!

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:38.970
5, 4, 3, 2, 1, fire!

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.840
The beam didn't work!

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:45.540
It's because of the ferric oxide storm.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:47.750
We won't make it in time!

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:49.610
Just leave this to me!

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:58.840
The storm is...

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:07.360
It's going blinky blink!

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.120
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:10.710
Can you hear me, Tamaki?

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:13.810
Izuru and Asagi are about to come 
out, so please retrieve their units.

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:16.410
You got it! Master Daneel is with them,

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.000
so I've just gotta save them!

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:22.010
I'm transferring the 
targets' coordinates.

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:23.520
They should emerge from the long hole.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:24.200
'Kay!

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.040
They followed their orders 
until they died...

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:52.450
Sounds just like us.

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:53.150
You're wrong.

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:57.670
We're clones made to follow orders 
and fight, just like them.

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.550
How are we any different 
from those soldiers?

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:07.250
We aren't blindly obeying orders.

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:10.390
Even if we were made to fight,

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:14.540
we're currently fighting because we 
felt that it was necessary, right?

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:25.160
What's going on?

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:28.120
Keep calm, Kitty. I'm on my way.

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:32.150
Maintain your current course, 
speed and angle of climb.

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:34.060
Mew-kay!

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:52.100
We've collected all of the units.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:52.830
And the data?

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.130
I memorized everything.

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:57.050
Thank goodness...

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:01.110
Not everything turned out great.

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:01.930
Huh?

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:07.750
What's the situation?!

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:09.450
The power reactor is melting down!

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:10.770
It'll go critical in five minutes!

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:14.360
The cockpit hatch's release bolts 
have been rendered inoperable.

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:16.270
The emergency hatch is broken!

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:22.460
Damn it! We're in Condition: Triple Red!

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:25.070
Do whatever you can to 
avoid Code: Dead End!

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.010
Roger!

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.040
Get the coolant!

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:41.130
It's hot! I'm dying...

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.540
Kitty, I'm sure you can take it.

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:45.050
We'll be sure to save you!

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.970
Okay! I'll hang in there!

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:00.070
This should do it!

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:14.500
Are you all right?

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:17.420
Who could that be...?

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:21.760
Is it Master Siegfried? 
Master Guiliano?

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.460
Or could it be...

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:25.700
...Master Daneel?!

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:37.980
Thank goodness!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:40.630
We did it, Bro!

00:21:46.270 --> 00:21:47.490
Thank you.

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:56.220
We successfully retrieved the data.

00:21:56.220 --> 00:21:57.900
Analyze it with all due haste.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:58.850
Roger.

00:21:59.940 --> 00:22:02.030
If we knew where their gate was...

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:55.990
"Secret Mission"
